<urn:atm:triage:finding/AW3-CI-006>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AW3-CI-006" ;
  triage:title "Just lint fails: al5_uds and ao2_plaintext_baseline architecture gates cannot find listener code after the AW3-QA-B5 module move to runtime_listener.rs" ;
  triage:description "PR #1182 at db47e09c9, Just lint (ubuntu-latest): atm-architecture boundary_enforcement fails 2 of 91: al5_uds_is_a_framework_adapter_over_the_one_client_and_router (boundary_enforcement.rs:2769, reads lib.rs + unix_socket.rs + http1_server.rs + client.rs by path and no longer sees the UDS lifecycle) and ao2_plaintext_baseline_stays_on_the_existing_direct_peer_pipeline (boundary_enforcement.rs:207, splits lib.rs on async fn bind_configured_direct_peer_listener and finds nothing). Cause: the AW3-QA-B5 pure module move relocated the listener code from crates/atm-http-runtime/src/lib.rs to the new crates/atm-http-runtime/src/runtime_listener.rs (127 lines), and these gates read source files by explicit path. Same defect class as AW3-CI-002. Reproduced locally at db47e09c9. Fix: make the gates read runtime_listener.rs (and router_support.rs where relevant) alongside lib.rs with every assertion left byte-for-byte unchanged, or move the listener code back; either way the gate assertions and their policy must not be relaxed, and the gate change goes through quality-mgr with a boundary-guard eye. Run the full just lint before pushing." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-aw" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "ci" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-05T05:58:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AW3 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-05T05:50:17Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
